            "selector": "impl[SessionTools<'a, D>]/fn[read_node]",
            "rationale": "Clause: \"During a `read_node` tool call, they are returned to the agent as a tool error\" and node inputs are presented \"using the returned value's `NodeContents::format`\". An alternative that gives the same results for simple domains but violates the clause: have the tool serialize node data, or fetch the text through a separate path such as direct source resolution, instead of `format()` on the value returned by `prepare_read`. Another violation: let a load failure abort the session instead of returning a tool error. `SessionTools::read_node` is a separate caller from `Ask::execute`. It prepares the read once and formats `snapshot.content.format()`. It records `Dependency::Node` with the snapshot's fingerprint. It returns failures as `io::Error`, which the tool layer reports as a tool error. The other proposed root does not cover this path."
          }
        ]
