        "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each observable obligation of `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering`.\n\n1. **Inputs are presented through the returned value's `format`.**\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix]` sets a custom formatter. It asserts that the serialized first user message contains `formatted input: source`.\n   - `fn[agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces]` uses `distinct_pages`. Its `ParallelConversations` provider asserts that the formatted page contents appear in the history for the `read_node` and `get_next_page` flow.\n   - `fn[behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer]` checks that the domain contents are delivered in queued order.\n   - `fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` checks that the contents reach the agent in queued order, including repeated nodes.\n   - `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]` and `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` assert `format()` output directly.\n\n2. **Text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.**\n   - The contracts test changes the underlying contents after the read. It then asserts that `snapshot.content.format()` still returns `before` and that `fingerprint()` still equals the snapshot fingerprint.\n   - The default-tool test asserts that the dependency fingerprint is `source`. It also asserts that the underlying node was read exactly once (`reads == [1]`) while the formatted text was delivered.\n   - The `explicit_insertions` test asserts that each read is recorded as a dependency with its fingerprint.\n\n3. **Load and prepare failures for queued builder inputs return `ValidationError::Graph`.**\n   - `validation_tests.rs#fn[queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation]` covers read failure (`Graph(\"read\")`), edge failure (`Graph(\"edges\")`) and preparation failure (`Graph(\"render\")`).\n   - It asserts that the agent is not invoked and that no dependency is recorded for the failed preparation.\n\n4. **Failures during a `read_node` tool call are returned to the agent as a tool error, and the agent can continue.**\n   - `fn[node_preparation_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents]` makes preparation fail.\n   - It asserts that the next request carries a `ToolResult` with `is_error`, the tool name `read_node` and the error text.\n   - It then asserts that the agent submits successfully and that no dependency is recorded.\n\nThe loading and preparation obligations that the subject delegates to `requirements.sdk.graph.node_content` are cited context. The `format` signature and retained-value obligations belong to `requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`. Neither needs separate assessment here. I found no unmet behavioral obligation and no marking gap."
