      "selector": "impl[Ask<'a, 'd, D, R, P>]#2/fn[execute]",
      "rationale": "Clause: \"The SDK presents node inputs using the returned value's `NodeContents::format`\" (`let contents = domain.node_content(&node_id)?; let text = contents.format();`), with failures of loading returned as `ValidationError::Graph` for inputs queued on an ask builder. No implementation edge exists. An alternative that keeps the observable behavior for simple domains but violates the clause: render queued inputs with `Debug`, or re-read the node via a second `node_content` call, or build text from a domain-specific accessor, instead of calling `format()` on the value returned by the same read that produced the fingerprint. `Ask::execute` is the root that performs this delegation. It calls `prepare_read` (mapping errors to `ValidationError::Graph`), calls `snapshot.content.format()`, and pairs the text with `snapshot.fingerprint` in `PreparedInput`. No other root covers the ask-builder path."
    },
